WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.410
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.680 --> 00:08.055
In the language of flowers, a black rose means

3
00:09.680 --> 00:12.305
"I will resent you till the day I die."

4
00:31.139 --> 00:35.722
5 CONTESTANTS LEFT. 4 DAYS AND 3 HOURS UNTIL THE GAME ENDS.

5
00:38.097 --> 00:42.389
PM 03:00 JST TOKYO

6
00:44.055 --> 00:48.972
"I have a gift for my players. Video conference in one hour."

7
00:49.722 --> 00:52.180
We have to access this link...

8
00:52.847 --> 00:54.097
What?!

9
00:54.222 --> 00:55.264
PM 02:00 SGT SINGAPORE

10
00:56.764 --> 00:58.139
One hour?!

11
01:00.805 --> 01:02.972
It's impossible...

12
01:06.597 --> 01:08.555
PM 03:00 JST NAHA

13
01:08.764 --> 01:11.222
"Participate or be disqualified."

14
01:28.014 --> 01:30.222
PM 02:00 HKT HONG KONG

15
01:30.930 --> 01:32.139
A "gift"?

16
01:32.639 --> 01:33.972
Another message?

17
01:34.555 --> 01:37.389
How dare they? Don't they know who I am?

18
01:39.930 --> 01:41.930
What does he want us to do?

19
01:44.055 --> 01:47.014
They're from that "GAME" thing on TV.

20
01:56.680 --> 01:57.847
Let's go.

21
02:10.264 --> 02:11.680
I bought it for tomorrow.

22
02:12.017 --> 02:14.513
-Tomorrow? -Did you forget?

23
02:15.180 --> 02:20.639
No way I'd forget. It's our... tenth.

24
02:57.173 --> 03:00.288
Even so, considering the scale,

25
03:00.403 --> 03:03.403
a crime syndicate must be behind it.

26
03:04.111 --> 03:08.496
We've also received some special footage. Please take a look.

27
03:09.111 --> 03:13.195
It was recorded moments ago in Teito TV's newsroom.

28
03:13.320 --> 03:18.403
The man in black is thought to belong to the criminal organization.

29
03:18.528 --> 03:20.236
However, the man...

30
03:20.361 --> 03:22.929
You promised not to use that footage.

31
03:22.986 --> 03:25.778
Is there anything misleading in it?

32
03:25.903 --> 03:30.070
It contains the truth. Reporting it is our job.

33
03:30.195 --> 03:34.278
People need to know how violent Toshiro Niide is.

34
03:34.445 --> 03:37.153
-Niide is... -Put your feelings aside!

35
03:38.903 --> 03:44.820
We're seeing a heinous, unprecedented, global kidnapping case.

36
03:44.945 --> 03:47.820
And you're stuck in the middle of it.

37
03:48.320 --> 03:52.445
Make the most of your journalistic good fortune.

38
03:59.445 --> 04:05.695
The man attacking him appears to be "Wrath," a police detective working in Tokyo,

39
04:05.820 --> 04:11.945
while the man in glasses accompanying him seems to be a doctor from Seoul.

40
04:12.570 --> 04:15.278
We're global celebrities now.

41
04:16.778 --> 04:18.653
How did we get here?

42
04:22.736 --> 04:27.528
The enemy's greater than we thought.

43
04:27.653 --> 04:31.195
They're enjoying watching us squirm.

44
04:33.570 --> 04:35.861
No matter who they are, Saori...

45
04:38.861 --> 04:41.111
everyone is coming home safe.

46
04:43.070 --> 04:43.903
That's our goal.

47
04:52.236 --> 04:55.445
2 MINUTES UNTIL THE VIDEO CONFERENCE

48
05:22.320 --> 05:27.070
Tokyo and Seoul, I see.

49
05:27.445 --> 05:30.861
Perhaps we should introduce ourselves.

50
05:31.028 --> 05:34.153
Toshiro Niide, Tokyo. Are you the Hong Kong player?

51
05:34.820 --> 05:39.653
I saw your video. You shouldn't resort to violence, detective.

52
05:48.361 --> 05:51.861
Her son Kuranosuke is a software engineer,

53
05:51.986 --> 05:53.903
fairly famous in IT circles.

54
05:55.236 --> 05:58.278
Can you trace the host?

55
06:01.361 --> 06:05.028
Please, we all need to work together.

56
06:08.070 --> 06:09.528
What's so funny?

57
06:11.358 --> 06:16.358
The criminal arranged this meeting, fully aware that we will discuss this.

58
06:16.483 --> 06:20.608
So, it's impossible to chase the host,

59
06:21.150 --> 06:23.483
even for a skilled software engineer.

60
06:24.566 --> 06:27.691
So you checked us out while hiding your own identity.

61
06:27.900 --> 06:30.650
Gotta hand it to you, shyster.

62
06:30.983 --> 06:33.066
That's a bit rich coming from you.

63
06:33.191 --> 06:34.316
What?!

64
06:35.816 --> 06:39.316
Sorry! Oh, I made it!

65
06:39.525 --> 06:41.358
Your connection isn't very good.

66
06:42.066 --> 06:44.275
I'm in a tunnel!

67
06:46.525 --> 06:50.191
You're the Tokyo guy, right? Thanks for your help.

68
06:50.650 --> 06:52.275
It's not like I...

69
06:52.525 --> 06:54.525
Guess what was the clue for my third checkpoint.

70
06:55.191 --> 06:57.525
"Climb towards the yellow rain."

71
06:57.691 --> 07:01.025
So, I've got no choice but to take the call here. If not, I'd run out of time.

72
07:01.525 --> 07:02.775
Awful, right?

73
07:04.650 --> 07:07.566
Hello?

74
07:07.858 --> 07:09.775
Oh, no! Hello?

75
07:10.650 --> 07:12.983
Ah, can you hear me now?

76
07:15.608 --> 07:18.191
Best not to talk about missions here.

77
07:19.941 --> 07:21.566
Why not?

78
07:22.650 --> 07:27.303
Yes, why not? "We need to work together," right? Don't we?

79
07:29.403 --> 07:30.070
Who are you?

80
07:30.596 --> 07:33.816
He's a lawyer from Hong Kong. Be careful what you say.

81
07:34.383 --> 07:35.150
To anyone.

82
07:52.983 --> 07:54.983
Is someone there? Show your face!

83
07:55.108 --> 07:58.775
Please, stop this madness and let Rian go, right now!

84
07:58.900 --> 08:04.025
Please, please let Tony go! I'll do whatever you want!

85
08:05.797 --> 08:08.047
I will warn you only once.

86
08:08.172 --> 08:12.089
Players who disrupt the game will be instantly disqualified.

87
08:15.297 --> 08:17.797
I will now distribute your gifts.

88
08:23.919 --> 08:28.426
What? This is our gift?

89
08:30.422 --> 08:33.710
One vote each. That's my gift to you.

90
08:36.797 --> 08:39.210
You may vote to eject a player from the game.

91
08:40.630 --> 08:45.964
The player with the most votes will be eliminated.

92
08:48.330 --> 08:53.396
Naturally, death awaits the loved one of player who is eliminated.

93
08:55.755 --> 09:01.005
Now, choose who among the five to eliminate.

94
09:45.755 --> 09:48.005
KIDNAP GAME

95
09:51.589 --> 09:57.380
Select the person to be eliminated from the designated site.

96
09:57.505 --> 10:00.964
The final vote is in 24 hours.

97
10:01.089 --> 10:05.297
Until then, you are free to keep revoting.

98
10:05.964 --> 10:09.380
You're asking us to eliminate someone?

99
10:09.656 --> 10:14.630
It's only the sixth day! You said the time limit was ten days!

100
10:14.876 --> 10:17.005
Why are you doing this to us?!

101
10:17.547 --> 10:21.255
So that it will be a fitting hell for your torment.

102
10:21.797 --> 10:23.922
What if we all vote for ourselves?

103
10:24.089 --> 10:27.380
Then we'd all have the same number of votes. What happens then?

104
10:27.908 --> 10:29.716
No one will be eliminated.

105
10:30.486 --> 10:34.035
Then to hell with voting! We just need to not vote.

106
10:38.422 --> 10:39.672
Kiju?

107
10:40.880 --> 10:43.755
Can you trust everyone here?

108
10:45.630 --> 10:47.172
Exactly.

109
10:47.422 --> 10:49.547
How could I trust strangers like you?

110
10:53.047 --> 10:55.214
We are faced with the prisoner's dilemma.

111
10:56.722 --> 10:57.576
What's that?

112
10:58.350 --> 11:02.422
Say there are two prisoners, A and B.

113
11:02.589 --> 11:06.303
To make them confess, a prosecutor offers each a plea bargain.

114
11:07.373 --> 11:09.206
There are three possible outcomes.

115
11:09.568 --> 11:12.417
Outcome one: both prisoners stay silent.

116
11:13.270 --> 11:16.380
Their sentences are reduced from five years to two.

117
11:16.640 --> 11:19.682
Outcome two: one of them confesses.

118
11:19.903 --> 11:23.636
He's set free, and the other is given a ten-year sentence.

119
11:24.370 --> 11:27.089
Outcome three: both of them confess...

120
11:27.410 --> 11:29.316
and both get five years in prison.

121
11:30.088 --> 11:32.515
So, what should the prisoners do?

122
11:38.563 --> 11:43.021
I mean, if they both stay silent, they only get two years... isn't that best?

123
11:43.146 --> 11:45.730
Yes, but both will confess.

124
11:45.855 --> 11:49.521
Because humans only care about themselves.

125
11:54.316 --> 11:56.364
That's how you play into the crook's hands!?

126
12:03.688 --> 12:06.521
This meeting will end when I exit.

127
12:06.980 --> 12:09.443
We will reconvene in 24 hours.

128
12:10.438 --> 12:11.850
Wait!

129
12:13.688 --> 12:19.050
What if someone completes their mission in the next 24 hours?

130
12:20.716 --> 12:23.750
The game will end, and there will be no vote.

131
12:26.343 --> 12:27.336
Understood.

132
12:34.188 --> 12:37.938
END OF VIDEO CONFERENCE

133
13:03.646 --> 13:08.490
What is this? Who am I supposed to vote for?

134
13:11.437 --> 13:15.923
They're so cocky... but nobody prevails over my talent, right?

135
13:16.755 --> 13:20.797
Good point. The most talented one will surely prevail.

136
13:26.813 --> 13:29.271
Information! Get me information!

137
14:44.436 --> 14:47.150
Mission? What mission?

138
14:47.175 --> 14:48.395
PM 04:26 KST

139
14:48.420 --> 14:52.426
They released a manifesto. There's no way you don't know.

140
14:53.596 --> 14:54.656
What do you mean?

141
14:55.343 --> 14:59.210
For your own sake as well.

142
15:07.177 --> 15:10.635
RETRIBUTION FOR PROFITEERING

143
15:10.760 --> 15:12.593
SUBPAR PRODUCTS

144
15:12.718 --> 15:15.056
DAUGHTER A VICTIM OF PARENTS' GREED

145
15:15.466 --> 15:17.423
We're victims. They took our daughter.

146
15:18.800 --> 15:20.943
Why are they attacking us?

147
15:21.677 --> 15:26.843
-Hurry up and find her! -Please leave.

148
15:43.468 --> 15:45.760
AYUN

149
16:38.260 --> 16:40.718
PREGNANCY AND CHILDBIRTH

150
16:48.343 --> 16:51.093
WHY MEN MUST SUPPORT THEIR PARTNERS

151
16:53.385 --> 16:55.260
Just hypothetically...

152
16:56.052 --> 16:59.427
If we had a baby, how about the name "Nozomi"?

153
18:26.683 --> 18:28.996
Sorry I couldn't cook anything.

154
18:36.197 --> 18:40.530
Your wife loved cooking, right?

155
18:42.941 --> 18:47.163
Yeah, she was always thinking of my health.

156
18:50.941 --> 18:52.482
What a wonderful wife.

157
18:54.899 --> 18:59.232
I caused her nothing but worry.

158
19:00.066 --> 19:02.149
When I considered quitting...

159
19:03.316 --> 19:06.857
Swear to me. That you'll do what's right.

160
19:07.857 --> 19:11.524
Put your anger aside. Show me your kindness...

161
19:12.566 --> 19:16.191
Kindness that shields the weak...

162
19:16.816 --> 19:23.899
That's the right thing for you to do.

163
19:25.441 --> 19:27.066
The "right thing."

164
19:27.816 --> 19:31.399
She comforted me, and supported me.

165
19:33.857 --> 19:40.357
But I never truly made the effort to understand her.

166
19:42.607 --> 19:44.482
She wanted a baby.

167
19:48.524 --> 19:54.774
But I was abused by my father when I was a child.

168
19:57.816 --> 20:00.566
I didn't know if I'd be a good dad.

169
20:04.107 --> 20:08.232
So I always brushed her comments aside.

170
20:10.357 --> 20:13.982
Hey, so... Just hypothetically...

171
20:14.357 --> 20:18.149
If we had a baby, how about the name "Nozomi"?

172
20:19.191 --> 20:24.232
-Nozomi? -Yeah, as in "hope."

173
20:24.524 --> 20:26.982
It'd work for a boy or a girl.

174
20:27.332 --> 20:29.903
Yeah, that's not bad.

175
20:36.243 --> 20:37.107
Yeah...

176
20:39.372 --> 20:41.831
In the future Saori dreamed of...

177
20:44.403 --> 20:46.028
we had a child.

178
20:49.774 --> 20:53.274
But even so, I...

179
21:01.732 --> 21:03.232
There's still time.

180
21:05.941 --> 21:10.066
You can still make her dream come true.

181
21:11.941 --> 21:16.482
That's what you're fighting so hard for, isn't it?

182
21:20.399 --> 21:21.357
Yeah.

183
21:23.982 --> 21:25.316
With you, right?

184
21:27.274 --> 21:28.566
In my case...

185
21:32.357 --> 21:33.691
Look at this.

186
21:35.857 --> 21:38.441
My wife is being slandered.

187
21:41.774 --> 21:44.149
She's called me several times.

188
21:46.941 --> 21:48.982
She's also messaged me.

189
21:51.147 --> 21:54.434
But I can't bear to look...

190
21:56.692 --> 21:58.983
Whatever it takes, do it!

191
22:02.649 --> 22:08.482
I don't know... what to do.

192
22:12.485 --> 22:16.350
I will complete my mission and save Rian, by any means possible.

193
22:20.190 --> 22:22.024
That's why you asked that?

194
22:22.316 --> 22:27.566
What if someone completes their mission in the next twenty-four hours?

195
22:36.118 --> 22:37.410
Think, Kiju!

196
22:38.405 --> 22:40.599
Save her and the rest will die!

197
22:40.624 --> 22:42.183
If I'm voted out, Rian...

198
22:42.208 --> 22:44.166
I won't let that happen.

199
22:44.770 --> 22:48.690
-Is someone else going to take the fall? -I won't let anyone die.

200
22:50.810 --> 22:52.774
Only if nobody votes.

201
22:53.770 --> 22:57.691
But someone will. And it only takes one.

202
23:01.941 --> 23:04.107
There's a worse possibility.

203
23:05.257 --> 23:05.937
What?

204
23:06.437 --> 23:09.790
The other three... Are they really just players?

205
23:10.883 --> 23:11.857
What do you mean?

206
23:12.382 --> 23:13.923
What if one is the mastermind?

207
23:14.590 --> 23:17.163
-You're overthinking. -What about you?

208
23:19.424 --> 23:23.382
What if you're waiting for everyone else to die?

209
23:24.924 --> 23:29.090
You said earlier that you were going to save Saori.

210
23:32.799 --> 23:34.674
It's only natural.

211
23:36.840 --> 23:40.090
You want to make her dream come true.

212
23:43.424 --> 23:48.507
I have Rian's dreams to protect.

213
23:50.590 --> 23:53.465
I couldn't save her sight.

214
23:55.632 --> 24:02.965
I have to make amends. My hands shake and I can't even grip the scalpel.

215
24:03.257 --> 24:04.590
But even so...

216
24:06.715 --> 24:08.965
Rian continues to play the cello.

217
24:09.090 --> 24:11.382
She dreams of being a cellist.

218
24:13.382 --> 24:14.283
Hope.

219
24:16.553 --> 24:20.403
She's my hope.

220
24:21.743 --> 24:22.993
I don't matter.

221
24:24.202 --> 24:29.343
I have to save Rian. For her sake, I'll...

222
24:29.415 --> 24:34.207
Kiju! Don't be hasty. We'll rescue all the hostages.

223
24:36.243 --> 24:37.618
Right?

224
24:55.160 --> 24:57.035
Saori!

225
25:00.827 --> 25:02.410
There's still time.

226
25:03.827 --> 25:07.368
You can still make her dream come true.

227
25:16.577 --> 25:21.743
ELIMINATION GAME 10 HOURS UNTIL THE VOTE COUNT

228
25:21.868 --> 25:23.660
AM 06:05 JST

229
25:49.285 --> 25:51.743
NOTIFICATION

230
26:53.839 --> 26:56.589
So, what language shall we speak?

231
26:58.214 --> 27:00.149
Any language is fine for me.

232
27:01.714 --> 27:03.255
How about Japanese?

233
27:04.255 --> 27:05.255
Sure.

234
27:06.339 --> 27:11.672
This is what some call a power spot. I've had my share of blessings.

235
27:12.255 --> 27:13.505
Get to the point.

236
27:13.964 --> 27:15.964
Sorry about yesterday.

237
27:16.880 --> 27:22.589
I had to hide my intentions from the mastermind.

238
27:23.380 --> 27:24.505
What intentions?

239
27:26.547 --> 27:32.643
Only one can prevail, but you're working together... Why?

240
27:35.386 --> 27:36.837
To save everyone.

241
27:37.339 --> 27:39.839
He agreed to help.

242
27:40.254 --> 27:41.730
Makes sense.

243
27:43.288 --> 27:45.872
I also want to save everyone.

244
27:48.835 --> 27:52.669
Then you'll help us?

245
27:53.089 --> 27:54.496
Of course I will.

246
27:56.047 --> 28:00.797
We're trying to find a common denominator that explains

247
28:00.922 --> 28:03.214
why the players were chosen.

248
28:03.672 --> 28:05.422
Any ideas?

249
28:07.297 --> 28:11.005
First, let's decide what to do about the vote.

250
28:13.630 --> 28:20.255
I propose that we join forces to eliminate players who pose a threat.

251
28:20.380 --> 28:24.464
We're going to save the hostages. We can't let anyone else die.

252
28:24.589 --> 28:28.714
All we can do is try to keep casualties to a minimum.

253
28:29.339 --> 28:33.339
You're proposing that the three of us kill someone?

254
28:33.880 --> 28:35.547
Yes, I am.

255
28:36.797 --> 28:39.589
-If I could, I'd have... -Kiju!

256
28:45.089 --> 28:46.505
Who would we choose?

257
28:51.089 --> 28:53.172
Who is the most dangerous?

258
28:53.714 --> 28:58.172
The flight attendant in Singapore doesn't pose a threat.

259
28:58.547 --> 29:02.672
That leaves one. Kuranosuke Higa in Naha.

260
29:03.130 --> 29:07.596
He's dangerous. His success came from betraying others.

261
29:07.755 --> 29:14.255
See how hated he is. He'd sacrifice you in a heartbeat.

262
29:14.880 --> 29:20.214
If someone deleted Christina's video, it must have been him.

263
29:20.630 --> 29:24.297
Then we vote him out. Agreed?

264
29:24.422 --> 29:27.672
Wait! His mother is being held hostage.

265
29:27.797 --> 29:31.547
She has cancer. She wouldn't live long anyway.

266
29:33.005 --> 29:39.214
The lives of your daughter and my sister are far more valuable.

267
29:41.297 --> 29:43.255
Well, that settles it.

268
29:45.028 --> 29:47.649
I'll see you at the vote count.

269
29:53.047 --> 29:54.672
You're okay with this?

270
29:58.547 --> 29:59.672
One more thing.

271
30:01.464 --> 30:05.964
As a fellow collaborator, I'd like to know your missions.

272
30:07.013 --> 30:08.180
What's yours?

273
30:08.591 --> 30:12.299
Oh, it's work-related. Like yours, probably.

274
30:15.964 --> 30:19.339
I'll tell you when the time comes.

275
30:20.297 --> 30:21.630
Likewise.

276
30:49.576 --> 30:53.005
Nobody stands in my way.

277
31:01.409 --> 31:04.382
To win a case, forget ideology, principles,

278
31:04.716 --> 31:07.174
and moral and ethical sensibilities.

279
31:07.323 --> 31:10.665
What about good and evil? Isn't our job to...

280
31:10.790 --> 31:13.124
True good and evil don't exist.

281
31:15.790 --> 31:18.999
Only information and analysis win cases.

282
31:26.785 --> 31:27.683
Sylvia...

283
31:28.624 --> 31:31.716
I want you to succeed in life, like me.

284
31:32.956 --> 31:34.956
Our parents would have felt the same.

285
31:36.063 --> 31:39.263
I know... Thank you.

286
31:53.165 --> 31:55.290
That lawyer might be right.

287
31:56.020 --> 31:57.343
You're voting for Higa?

288
31:57.377 --> 31:59.877
If not, you might be eliminated.

289
32:00.750 --> 32:02.582
What about saving everyone?

290
32:04.999 --> 32:09.082
You just want to win, don't you?

291
32:10.040 --> 32:12.540
Is this the "right thing"?

292
32:15.165 --> 32:18.915
It seems it was a mistake to team up with you.

293
32:20.665 --> 32:23.332
I won't let them kill Higa's mother!

294
32:26.874 --> 32:28.124
Kiju!

295
32:35.457 --> 32:39.582
ELIMINATION GAME 4 HOURS UNTIL THE VOTE COUNT

296
32:59.457 --> 33:03.540
I NEED TO DISCUSS SOMETHING WITH YOU. PLEASE CALL ME. HAN KIJU

297
33:11.082 --> 33:12.176
Is that you, Higa?

298
33:15.186 --> 33:15.696
Yes.

299
33:16.769 --> 33:20.790
The lawyer, Andy... He plans to vote you out.

300
33:21.207 --> 33:24.665
He approached me and Niide about it.

301
33:24.915 --> 33:27.915
But I refused.

302
33:29.624 --> 33:35.463
I can't help you, but I wanted you to know.

303
33:36.430 --> 33:40.410
Got it. Thanks.

304
33:49.707 --> 33:54.332
Also, I heard about your mother.

305
33:57.707 --> 34:04.082
If I'm alive when this game's over,

306
34:05.832 --> 34:07.832
let me examine her.

307
34:10.275 --> 34:10.996
Bye.

308
34:12.138 --> 34:13.221
Wait!

309
34:17.143 --> 34:18.957
He's targeting you, not me.

310
34:22.161 --> 34:25.995
Before you wrote to me, I got a message from Andy.

311
34:26.447 --> 34:29.656
"I have discovered what Kiju's mission is.

312
34:29.781 --> 34:32.072
"He could easily complete it.

313
34:32.447 --> 34:37.322
"Let's work together. He must be eliminated first."

314
34:39.572 --> 34:41.864
Your mission is to kill a patient?

315
34:43.197 --> 34:44.822
Commit murder.

316
34:45.031 --> 34:48.531
You could do it whenever you feel like it.

317
34:48.822 --> 34:53.197
Andy sent Singapore the same message.

318
34:53.447 --> 34:56.031
Wait, please!

319
34:56.281 --> 35:02.822
No! Please, my daughter... Rian...

320
35:03.364 --> 35:06.114
You have two votes even if I abstain.

321
35:09.447 --> 35:13.281
Could you vote for Andy? I'll ask Niide,

322
35:13.406 --> 35:18.322
that'll make three.

323
35:18.447 --> 35:20.365
So you'll vote for the lawyer?

324
35:23.156 --> 35:25.225
You're fine killing Andy's sister?

325
35:26.697 --> 35:29.114
I thought you couldn't kill.

326
35:30.989 --> 35:33.281
Sorry, I'm not cooperating.

327
35:48.364 --> 35:52.406
ELIMINATION GAME

328
36:13.197 --> 36:15.281
NOTIFICATION

329
36:33.031 --> 36:34.864
I spoke to the police.

330
36:34.989 --> 36:37.906
No doubt you are in dire straits.

331
36:38.739 --> 36:40.989
I know you don't want to kill.

332
36:41.114 --> 36:47.114
But please remember that Rian is everything to us.

333
36:47.364 --> 36:49.489
Her happiness is everything.

334
36:50.531 --> 36:52.364
She is all that matters.

335
36:52.531 --> 36:55.239
I can be the wife of a murderer.

336
36:56.114 --> 37:02.322
So save Rian, I beg you.

337
37:07.822 --> 37:12.156
All right... All right.

338
37:30.998 --> 37:33.748
WE NEED TO TALK. MEET ME AT THE SHRINE.

339
37:54.857 --> 37:57.482
-Here he comes. -Mr. Niide!

340
37:58.857 --> 38:03.149
Where are you going, Mr. Niide? What's your mission?

341
38:03.274 --> 38:06.607
No comment. Let me through.

342
38:06.732 --> 38:09.691
-Please answer me. -Leave, now!

343
38:12.732 --> 38:16.332
Mr. Niide, what's your sin? What did you do?

344
38:16.423 --> 38:19.007
-Are you enjoying your fame? -Move.

345
38:19.132 --> 38:21.623
Violence again? I'm a pacifist!

346
38:22.493 --> 38:28.368
Those are the eyes of a dangerous man! "Wrath"! Eyes filled with rage!

347
38:31.660 --> 38:32.543
Leave.

348
38:39.990 --> 38:43.365
ELIMINATION GAME 1 HOUR UNTIL THE VOTE COUNT

349
38:58.691 --> 38:59.857
What's this about?

350
39:00.607 --> 39:02.982
You're conspiring against me.

351
39:03.649 --> 39:05.691
You did well to find that out.

352
39:06.590 --> 39:08.340
It doesn't matter anymore.

353
39:11.774 --> 39:16.543
No. It's you who is eliminated.

354
39:22.603 --> 39:25.519
Threatening me won't change the vote, doctor.

355
39:25.978 --> 39:28.103
This is not about vote.

356
39:28.478 --> 39:30.223
This is about saving my daughter.

357
39:30.715 --> 39:32.257
So, are you going to kill me?

358
39:32.603 --> 39:34.603
Yeah. Why not?

359
39:35.103 --> 39:38.269
Interesting. Do it.

360
39:40.769 --> 39:43.394
Come on. Do it.

361
39:44.478 --> 39:45.394
Do it!

362
39:49.103 --> 39:53.394
You can't. You can't kill. You just can't.

363
39:57.811 --> 40:00.769
It has been like that. Until now!

364
40:01.269 --> 40:06.019
So are you ready to bring death to my innocent sister, Mrs. Niide and others?

365
40:06.561 --> 40:10.686
That's right. Or only my daughter will die.

366
40:10.853 --> 40:14.103
And how will your daughter's future look like if she lives?

367
40:15.478 --> 40:19.061
How much colder and darker will her future be

368
40:19.644 --> 40:21.811
when her father's in jail for murder?

369
40:21.978 --> 40:24.394
Do you honestly think you're capable of giving her a worthwhile...

370
40:24.519 --> 40:25.769
Shut up!

371
40:31.478 --> 40:33.436
Rian has a dream.

372
40:35.186 --> 40:37.269
I don't care what happens to me.

373
40:39.269 --> 40:41.644
I'll save Rian, no matter what!

374
40:43.144 --> 40:44.894
Kiju, stop!

375
40:45.144 --> 40:47.478
-Let go! -Don't do it!

376
40:54.311 --> 40:55.728
So they were your thugs.

377
40:56.103 --> 40:57.811
You're late, detective.

378
41:00.019 --> 41:03.228
Did you get the part where Han Kiju tried to kill me?

379
41:03.519 --> 41:05.144
Yes, I did, sir.

380
41:05.353 --> 41:08.063
Send copies to Naha and Singapore at once.

381
41:08.678 --> 41:12.063
Now everyone is going to vote for you.

382
41:13.686 --> 41:17.394
-No! No! I have to kill him! -Kiju!

383
41:17.561 --> 41:21.516
You see? I called you to come here to see his true nature.

384
41:23.353 --> 41:26.686
I JUST RECEIVED A MESSAGE FROM A MAN FROM SEOUL TO COME TO THE SHRINE.

385
41:27.728 --> 41:32.603
-Niide, please, let me go... -Stop!

386
41:32.769 --> 41:36.728
If you don't want your wife to die, you'd better watch him until the vote.

387
41:37.853 --> 41:42.561
-Come on! I'll kill you! -Kiju!

388
42:18.311 --> 42:24.811
It's all your fault... Why... Why?!

389
42:47.519 --> 42:51.894
It's hopeless...

390
43:10.171 --> 43:13.879
I'm sorry, Rian...

391
43:20.894 --> 43:22.603
Let me die!

392
43:23.686 --> 43:27.728
If I die, Rian will be saved!

393
43:27.978 --> 43:29.686
It's not over yet!

394
43:31.061 --> 43:35.149
I can't trust what you say anymore... I don't believe you!

395
43:36.896 --> 43:39.061
You don't have to trust me.

396
43:39.186 --> 43:42.490
But do as I say.

397
43:43.119 --> 43:49.823
Vote to eliminate me. Whatever you do, just vote for me.

398
44:27.437 --> 44:30.562
ELIMINATION GAME 1 MINUTE UNTIL THE VOTE COUNT

399
44:31.106 --> 44:33.606
PM 03:59 JST

400
45:02.985 --> 45:05.544
It's time. Cast your votes.

401
45:06.482 --> 45:09.818
The player with the most votes will be eliminated.

402
45:48.819 --> 45:50.735
Let the tally begin.

403
46:28.152 --> 46:29.652
So much for teamwork.

404
46:38.110 --> 46:39.902
You double-crosser...

405
46:56.485 --> 46:59.069
Hey! Why me?!

406
47:05.610 --> 47:08.860
The player with the most votes will be eliminated.

407
47:52.319 --> 47:55.027
This is your doing, isn't it? Toshiro Niide.

408
47:55.985 --> 47:57.277
What do you mean?

409
47:59.777 --> 48:03.089
Why did you lie to me?! You said we'd all vote for the computer guy!

410
48:03.676 --> 48:10.944
Niide, I voted for Andy because I expected you and Kiju to do the same.

411
48:11.235 --> 48:12.527
What's going on?

412
48:15.694 --> 48:18.363
We can't afford for more players to be eliminated!

413
48:19.016 --> 48:22.325
More hostages will die! This was the only solution.

414
48:26.226 --> 48:29.726
Andy, I knew from the start that you'd make contact.

415
48:31.194 --> 48:34.110
And I knew from what you say, that you'd vote for Kiju.

416
48:37.069 --> 48:41.110
Kiju didn't want to vote for anyone. That's why I made him vote for me.

417
48:41.235 --> 48:43.152
And I voted for Janice.

418
48:43.444 --> 48:46.694
That gave the three of us one vote each.

419
48:47.652 --> 48:49.652
I asked Janice to vote for Higa.

420
48:49.944 --> 48:53.360
Janice, I have one request.

421
48:53.485 --> 48:56.652
Yes. And you tried to kick me out!

422
48:57.069 --> 49:00.152
If someone else voted for me, Tony would die!

423
49:00.777 --> 49:03.569
I tried to be kind because you helped me and this is how you repay me?!

424
49:04.027 --> 49:05.944
I knew nobody would vote for you.

425
49:06.194 --> 49:09.902
But... but...

426
49:12.027 --> 49:14.569
How'd you know I'd vote for Andy.

427
49:14.694 --> 49:18.569
Kiju doesn't want your mother to die. He was bound to contact you.

428
49:18.735 --> 49:22.402
Andy plots to sabotage others while Kiju tries to save them.

429
49:22.527 --> 49:28.319
I asked myself, who would you trust? Who would you keep around?

430
49:30.860 --> 49:34.527
You can't eliminate anyone... it's a tie.

431
49:35.735 --> 49:36.610
Indeed.

432
49:37.319 --> 49:38.485
We won.

433
49:40.152 --> 49:44.735
If you had lost, you would have been spared the hell that's to come.

434
49:46.110 --> 49:51.196
You are rivals. Mortal enemies in a fight to the death.

435
49:52.770 --> 49:57.110
Take a good, long look now. Before you kill each other.

436
49:57.819 --> 50:03.944
Enjoy your prisoner's dilemma. The elimination game has just begun!

437
50:09.235 --> 50:14.110
Niide... So you don't have the guts to sacrifice someone.

438
50:15.360 --> 50:17.985
Andy, I need to ask you something!

439
50:18.319 --> 50:22.556
Did you represent a driver who died in Tokyo five years ago?

440
50:25.756 --> 50:29.532
Answer me! This could lead to the Mastermind.

441
50:29.557 --> 50:33.515
An event from five years ago may connect us.

442
50:34.790 --> 50:36.290
I don't remember.

443
50:37.748 --> 50:42.123
What about you two? Were you in Tokyo five years ago?

444
50:42.707 --> 50:43.790
No.

445
50:43.998 --> 50:44.729
Me neither.

446
50:45.915 --> 50:48.873
You're just trying to find the Mastermind to complete your mission.

447
50:49.064 --> 50:53.481
No! Niide's trying to do what's right!

448
50:55.582 --> 50:59.665
He's doing it for us! He's trying to rescue the hostages!

449
51:02.457 --> 51:06.910
Look, we got through this predicament thanks to him.

450
51:08.373 --> 51:13.915
He's shown that if we work together, we can beat that criminal!

451
51:14.123 --> 51:20.623
He's shown that we can save our loved ones!

452
51:24.998 --> 51:29.040
You're right... We won this time.

453
51:38.780 --> 51:40.323
I guess I should thank you.

454
51:43.270 --> 51:44.249
Thanks.

455
52:13.915 --> 52:15.540
This is a nice spot.

456
52:17.582 --> 52:18.790
Yeah.

457
52:20.957 --> 52:23.040
When did you think of it?

458
52:25.165 --> 52:27.123
Dunno...

459
52:30.087 --> 52:32.835
I was just looking for the "right thing."

460
52:40.887 --> 52:42.856
You had me fooled.

461
52:46.156 --> 52:47.582
Sorry.

462
52:50.123 --> 52:55.915
Andy might have been watching, and you had lost your cool.

463
52:58.665 --> 53:00.040
I know...

464
53:00.873 --> 53:07.540
But no lies or secrets from now on.

465
53:16.429 --> 53:17.348
Sure.

466
53:20.157 --> 53:22.323
Let's get through this together.

467
53:23.196 --> 53:23.957
Yeah.

468
53:31.683 --> 53:32.516
Niide?

469
53:37.863 --> 53:43.582
I think our moves are being anticipated.

470
53:50.109 --> 53:51.415
By the mastermind?

471
53:52.957 --> 53:54.290
Yeah.

472
54:08.728 --> 54:13.082
It's like someone's predicting and countering my every move.

473
54:14.123 --> 54:16.498
Even so, you won this time.

474
54:17.582 --> 54:19.165
This time, yeah...

475
54:31.373 --> 54:32.707
Don't move!

476
54:34.915 --> 54:38.040
Is this guy's life worth a lot?
